# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# tuning/ — Terraform
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# State. This is the single most important line in this file. Terraform state
# is a plaintext record of everything it built, and for some resource types it
# contains secrets that were never secret in the .tf files themselves. It is
# also the thing that makes `terraform destroy` possible — lose it and you own
# orphaned cloud resources that quietly eat the Always Free quota.
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
.terraform.tfstate.lock.info

# The provider plugin cache — hundreds of MB of downloaded binaries that
# `terraform init` recreates on demand. Never belongs in git.
.terraform/

# Real variable values: OCIDs, key fingerprints, key paths, my home IP.
# The committed template is tuning/terraform.tfvars.example.
*.tfvars
*.tfvars.json
!*.tfvars.example

# Saved plan files are binary and can embed variable values.
*.tfplan
crash.log
crash.*.log

# .terraform.lock.hcl is deliberately NOT ignored — it pins provider versions
# and hashes, and committing it is what makes builds reproducible for anyone
# who clones this.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# rehearsal/ — Ansible
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The generated inventory holds the live public IP and my SSH key path.
# The committed template is rehearsal/inventory.example.ini.
rehearsal/inventory.ini
*.retry

# The kubeconfig orchestra pulls back from the node. This is a CREDENTIAL — it
# embeds a client certificate with cluster-admin rights on the cluster, and
# anyone holding it owns everything running there. Committing it would be the
# single worst mistake available in this repo.
rehearsal/kubeconfig*
kubeconfig
kubeconfig.*
*.kubeconfig

# Collections installed from requirements.yml. Reinstallable, not source.
rehearsal/collections/
rehearsal/*.log

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# backstage/ — secrets
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The age private key. SOPS-encrypted files are safe to commit *because* this
# never is. Belongs in ~/.config/sops/age/, not here — this pattern is a
# tripwire for the day I get careless.
*.agekey
key.txt
age-key.txt

# Anything decrypted for local use. Only *.enc.yaml belongs in git.
*.dec.yaml
*.dec.yml

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Keys and credentials, anywhere in the tree
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.pem
*.key
!**/*.pub
oci_api_key*
.oci/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# score/ — Go
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# `go build` drops the compiled binary next to the source, named after the
# module directory. It's ~6 MB of statically linked output that is regenerated
# from source in seconds — and the whole point of `score` is that binaries come
# from the pipeline, not from someone's laptop.
score/overture
score/overture.exe

# Coverage profiles from `go test -coverprofile`.
*.out
coverage.*

# Go workspace files are local-machine state, not project configuration.
go.work
go.work.sum

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# maestro/ — Python
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/

# pytest writes a self-ignoring .gitignore inside its own cache, so this
# line is redundant today. It is here because that behaviour is pytest's to
# change, and a stray cache directory in a commit is a silly way to find out
# that it did.
.pytest_cache/

# Holds MAESTRO_TOKEN — the same value backstage encrypts for Alertmanager.
# The committed template is maestro/.env.example.
.env
maestro/.env

# The notes maestro writes. They quote production logs verbatim, which is
# exactly the content this platform is arranged not to publish.
maestro/notes.md
notes.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor and OS noise
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
